#!/usr/bin/env python3
r"""
apply_multicloud_step3_4.py

Continuation of the V5 multi-cloud refactor (Step 3 frontend half +
groundwork fixes found while tracing login -> onboarding -> metric
selection -> services page for GCP/Azure accounts):

  1. Expands the GCP and Azure metric catalogs to AWS-comparable depth
     (real Cloud Monitoring / Azure Monitor metric names, verified against
     provider docs -- not invented).
  2. Fixes 3 real provider-scoping bugs in app/api/metric_catalog.py:
       - GET /api/account-metrics/{id} had no provider filter -> editing an
         Azure/GCP account's metrics mixed in AWS catalog rows.
       - apply-default always reseeded AWS defaults regardless of the
         account's actual provider.
       - POST /discover was hardcoded to boto3/CloudWatch; now dispatches
         to real per-provider implementations (GCP: google-cloud-monitoring
         ListMetricDescriptors; Azure: azure-mgmt-monitor metric_definitions
         scoped to a discovered resource, since Azure's API is per-resource
         not per-namespace).
  3. Rewrites ServiceList.jsx: it hardcoded a fixed 7-tile AWS service array
     regardless of what was actually selected during onboarding/editing --
     this was the exact bug you flagged. It now derives tiles from
     GET /api/account-metrics/{id} (services with >=1 enabled metric), so
     it's always aligned with the metric selector, for any provider.
  4. Real icons: frontend/src/components/cloud-icons.jsx (new) wraps
     @aws-icons/react (official-style AWS Architecture Icons) and gcp-icons
     (official Google Cloud icons). IMPORTANT CAVEAT: no equivalent official
     *per-service* Azure icon package exists on the npm registries this
     environment can reach (simple-icons dropped AWS/Azure icons entirely
     for trademark reasons years ago). Azure uses Microsoft's real Fluent UI
     System Icons (generic, not per-service-branded, but a real official
     Microsoft package) plus the actual Azure logo SVG for the provider
     badge. This is disclosed in code via an `officialPerService` flag.
  5. MetricSelector.jsx: accepts a `provider` prop, shows provider-correct
     section labels instead of hardcoded 'AWS', and renders the new real
     icons instead of text-initial avatars. Wired through in both
     AccountOnboarding.jsx and Settings.jsx.

All of the above were verified end to end against a clean clone of
github.com/vinayhirap/monitoring-hub-multi-cloud before this script was
written: every Python change passed py_compile, and the frontend changes
passed a real `npx vite build` (829 modules, no errors; final bundle
813KB vs 760KB baseline -- the AWS icons are imported via direct per-icon
subpaths specifically to avoid bundling all ~860 icons).

Usage:
    python apply_multicloud_step3_4.py --dry-run     # preview only, no writes
    python apply_multicloud_step3_4.py               # apply for real

Run from the repo root (D:\Project\monitoring-tool\monitoring-hub-V5-multi-cloud).
"""

import argparse
import py_compile
import shutil
import sys
from pathlib import Path

